## Problem

Rule 11 asserted only that each separator was present, not that each appeared exactly once. A slice-aliasing bug in a downstream consumer was producing tickets with duplicate `--- body ---` separators that passed validation and were committed to git.

## Fix

- `parseErg`: count occurrences of each separator (`LogSepCount`, `BodySepCount` fields on `Erg`)
- `validateErg`: fail when either count > 1, naming the offending separator
- `rules/tickets.md`: rule 11 wording updated from "both present" to "exactly once each"

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `validateErg` returns an error when `--- log ---` appears more than once
- [ ] `validateErg` returns an error when `--- body ---` appears more than once
- [ ] Two new test cases in `tests/test_validate.sh` cover both variants
- [ ] `make test` passes (all validate + ready + archive cases)
- [ ] `erg validate tickets/` on this repo returns clean
